 say the Berlin marketing executive used her political and military contacts to help a Russian intelligence officer gain access to influential circles and seek information on German defense policy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India women's team refuse Asia Cup cricket trophy from Pakistan minister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a2030d62e45bd6b21609c55f84755a2ec44a3d0cbe6c07b809fe59c536a7382</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:06:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-women-s-team-refuse-asia-cup-cricket-trophy-from-pakistan-minister/live-79254950--b1dfe4fc6375.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-women-s-team-refuse-asia-cup-cricket-trophy-from-pakistan-minister/live-79254950?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's women's cricket team skipped the trophy presentation with Pakistani minister Mohsin Naqvi after beating Sri Lanka to win a record eighth Asia Cup title.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pay to ghost your boss: Japan's resignation business</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dca1255d6c8ba0be9beebf085155e4485133c9053fcd5def389645d48a64199</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584--1937a091cd92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Resignation agencies in Japan help employees leave their jobs seamlessly in just 15 minutes. Young people are especially eager to use their services.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli minister accuses 'NAZA' filmmakers of 'treason'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a68754efb663cb57c61f25c6e3b982894040e6d9948eada2e0433c2422b1ced</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-minister-accuses-naza-filmmakers-of-treason/a-79255860--3831f9d14cfb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-minister-accuses-naza-filmmakers-of-treason/a-79255860?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israel's culture minister wants to strip the makers of a documentary on Israel's Gaza offensive of their citizenship. He accused the two of seeking "applause from antisemites around the world."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Finland: EU leaders meet to forge new Arctic policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96236decc48c47eca07e38065f4807f1e7a441f89319a7869b42a3d856dd6ab6</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T09:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/finland-eu-leaders-meet-to-forge-new-arctic-policy/a-79256956--5305e169dba5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/finland-eu-leaders-meet-to-forge-new-arctic-policy/a-79256956?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European leaders are meeting over shipping, resources and security in the region amid pressure from the US, China and Russia. The EU sees the Arctic as key to its future security as melting ice makes it more accessible.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea says recent drill shows 'huge destructive power'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92f859dfb1e7f734a402cc71deb3c7784016c87828fcd63c3b5c809e410736d6</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T08:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-says-recent-drill-shows-huge-destructive-power/a-79255028--00809ed0f8d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-says-recent-drill-shows-huge-destructive-power/a-79255028?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea carried out a coordinated live-fire exercise involving multiple weapons systems over the weekend. The drill came after the US, South Korea and Japan wrapped up five days of joint maritime exercises.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Iran replace sea trade with land routes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f4fba9209d629d0d151158779d140f788c6328a79f52ef9921b0fe59cae5f37</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T07:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179--9748aa6cdc36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran is shifting trade toward northern ports and land routes as its southern shipping faces a US blockade. Analysts say the corridors can keep essential goods moving, but cannot replace maritime trade.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>In cosmopolitan Berlin, elections still closed to foreigners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ed74ab8945055e505808507fd07420a1cd0de56855c1cd21e31729e01be3c5e</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579--2c7a3b66c58f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter of Berlin residents will have no say in the German capital's city-state election because they lack citizenship. That's the highest proportion of residents excluded from the election yet, and many are unhappy.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Canada seeks 'unique alliance' with EU, Carney says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:937da8beb86ef4db0e55224aeed23a366fe8b7a6015b85aab287a23fab39b111</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T06:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-seeks-unique-alliance-with-eu-carney-says/a-79254541--f7711865b23b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-seeks-unique-alliance-with-eu-carney-says/a-79254541?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mark Carney clarified Canada's EU ambitions amid a WSJ report that Ottawa was exploring an "associate membership" with the bloc.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Merz's CDU comes out on top in Lower Saxony polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8c8cde205c6bf6402b5d91a91dce39c394f5d9aea26da13019d2cf478280d9f</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T06:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-merz-s-cdu-comes-out-on-top-in-lower-saxony-polls/a-79254724--04c4d8ef8565.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-merz-s-cdu-comes-out-on-top-in-lower-saxony-polls/a-79254724?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Christian Democrats have emerged as the strongest party following local elections in the state of Lower Saxony. The vote was closely watched as an indicator of the strength of the far-right AfD, which came in third.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Cuban dance teacher ordered EU sabotage attacks from Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49ef0e0da866382ff5fc98ecd7903b6c0b7f1bd23260da49a3f53c574dbe55d6</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:07:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T05:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cuban-dance-teacher-ordered-eu-sabotage-attacks-from-russia/a-79225946--98bd6301770b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cuban-dance-teacher-ordered-eu-sabotage-attacks-from-russia/a-79225946?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 2024, a Cuban man coordinated a series of arson attacks in four EU countries while operating on behalf of Russian intelligence services. DW Investigations tracked him back to a Latin dance studio in Russia.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Trump dismisses report China supplied intel to Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aae3428629f083ee784b53c93406dd920e0a3f0581bdd4a2cc8c88f747404138</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T03:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-dismisses-report-china-supplied-intel-to-iran/a-79254419--2aca1e3ae2d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-dismisses-report-china-supplied-intel-to-iran/a-79254419?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president downplayed reports that Chinese entities had given Iran satellite imagery before a strike on a military base in Jordan that killed three American soldiers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden election 'very close' as left bloc claims tight lead</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f292fca2da0dfede822e3b5f9f82c0906399f896dc98b80300a7425efa9fc8b7</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T02:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sweden-election-very-close-as-left-bloc-claims-tight-lead/a-79248599--5c26e071ae25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sweden-election-very-close-as-left-bloc-claims-tight-lead/a-79248599?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The center-left opposition is narrowly ahead of the incumbent's right-wing bloc and could be poised to return to government after four years. The far-right Sweden Democrats surprisingly lost ground.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: CDU ahead in Lower Saxony local election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03a3951c9040a401bb1507701e0a1d4df5bcab4ab2948c575639b07184545293</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T00:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-ahead-in-lower-saxony-local-election/live-79223427--aff1c7ebec22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-cdu-ahead-in-lower-saxony-local-election/live-79223427?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The CDU is on course to win in municipal polls in the northwestern state of Lower Saxony that were seen as a gauge of support for the far-right AfD party.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Zverev wins US Open in golden year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dfff1a9992cca3a9f60ee8644ae04aad4d9b3561253e220c0dc6060285fb65b6</id><updated>2026-09-14T15:05:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T22:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706--d962ccd6a0c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev has won the US Open for the first time, defeating Ben Shelton in the final. It is Zverev's second Grand Slam win of 2026 after a long wait for his first title, but controversy still hangs over him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
